! name=all-inputs trig=ticks:0 restart
# Every input of the script format, one frame line per group, in the canonical order the writer
# spells its tokens. The `#` comment marker is the DSL's own (`docs/SCRIPT_DSL.md` §1).
0 a
1 x
2 y
3 b
4 lt
5 rt
6 lb
7 rb
8 r
9 lr
10 ax
11 du
12 dd
13 dl
14 cd
15 wk
16 esc
17 ok
18 mu
19 md
20 ml
21 mr
# One token can stand for two inputs, and a duration lights the whole run.
22 by
23 by:3
# The left stick, in both of its forms: a compass angle, and exact axes.
30 ls:0:10
42 ls:90:5
50 lsx:-1000:4
56 lsy:-1000:4
60 lsx:500:2 lsy:-500:2
# The right stick is the camera, with its own magnitudes.
70 rs:180:3
75 rsx:800:5
82 rsy:-1200:5
# Durations on ordinary tokens, and two tokens on one frame.
90 lt:10 x:4
# A walk bit, which the game reads as a magnitude rather than a key.
110 wk:20
